description:
FOUND s494g (Opus, 2026-09-25) while splicing the companion (t/lib/croak.t produced 0 of perl's 225 rows: `aborted-forms:1: Can't identify pragma to test from file name '' at common.pl`).  NOT caused by s494g: identical on a dc20a721 extraction (probed).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3 vs PCL):

    # a.pl
    require "./b.pl"; print "done\n";
    # b.pl
    my @c = caller;
    print scalar(@c), " [", join("|", map { defined ? $_ : "U" } @c), "]\n";
    1;

  perl: 3 [main|a.pl|1]
  PCL : 0 []

`caller` with no argument at the TOP LEVEL of a required file must answer the frame of the `require` (package, requiring file, line).  PCL answers the empty list (a caller inside a sub in the same file works).  t/lib/common.pl reads `my (undef, $file) = caller;` to derive the pragma name from the .t file name, so every t/lib/*.t driver that uses common.pl (croak.t; likely others, never measured -- t/lib/ is outside the --all population) aborts at its first line.  Member of the caller() fidelity family (#233, USER s488: bug queue) but a distinct mechanism: the require frame is not a sub frame.
Row cost: t/lib/croak.t 225 rows (snapshot row spliced s494g as a first measurement; baselines/row-shortfall.tsv t/lib/croak.t carries this task).
